so right now we're partnering with a  really fascinating project called  cold stack and they're doing some really  cool things in the world of cloud  storage in particular decentralized  cloud storage i want to tell you what  they're up to  how they're changing what's possible  when it comes to storing your files on  decentralized cloud networks and what  else they have  on the horizon so to start with  centralized  cloud storage most of us are familiar  with it many of us use it  daily weekly amazon web services  google cloud google drive you're paying  a company to store your data  on a centralized server but with  decentralized cloud storage the data is  distributed into different  pieces and stored in different  nodes of a peer-to-peer network and  there's many advantages  to the decentralization of cloud storage  more security because decentralized  storage platforms break apart user files  and distribute them across the network  and because the data scattered across  multiple nodes  there's no single point of failure your  files  being broken apart like this also means  more privacy because it's harder  to assemble that data back together and  decentralized networks are also  excellent for storing cold data meaning  data that's rarely used  but has to be stored a long time which  makes up about 60  of the world's data in fact so there are  a lot of different benefits to storing  data on a decentralized network like  this  but there are also some huge problems  facing the decentralized cloud storage  industry right now people have trouble  integrating them with their own systems  it can be expensive to get involved with  decentralized cloud storage networks can  be difficult to combine  and it's also difficult to switch  between them and a lot of this  is because there's no programming  interfaces  that unify all of the biggest  decentralized cloud  networks so developers can't reuse  existing tools to build on to what other  developers have already done  so these are the problems in essence  that cold stack is trying to solve  cold stack is an aggregator of all  decentralized clouds that already exist  and  cold stack thinks of themselves sort of  as the uber  for cloud storage cold stack lets  companies migrate from services like  amazon to decentralized clouds  with really what's just two clicks and  this lets users  save money when storing data it allows  users to save time and  effort when onboarding switching  combining these clouds  and there's no need for data migration  when you're switching between clouds  everything just stays really simple  there's a unified programming interface  and it makes things really easy for  developers as well  the cold stack ai selects the best cloud  to fit a user's needs and to optimize  the final storage cost  in an all-in-one platform and coldstack  is also 100 compatible with  amazon s3 api which is going to be  really useful for a lot of people  because it will allow any project  already using the amazon library or the  sdk  to quickly scale up and start using cold  stack with very little effort  and it also has a built-in option to  tokenize any file you've uploaded so you  can turn your files into nfts  and it has a universal digital asset  storage  for any nft marketplace so like i  mentioned  decentralized clouds especially good for  storing cold data  that's what cold stack does really well  and cold stack can do it for a fraction  of the cost  so let's really look at the advantages  of cold stack  over other clouds and also how they  price their services let's say you're a  company  for one year you need to store a million  files that are each one kilobyte  and also 10 000 files which are each one  gigabyte  during that year you're downloading  about 20  of those files our weave would cost you  about a hundred and ninety thousand  dollars our weave stores data  permanently which has advantages  but the cost can really add up for large  files  sia would cost you about fifteen hundred  dollars  amazon glacier would be about eight  hundred and two dollars and  cold stack would be only four hundred  dollars  cold stacks ai pipeline finds the best  storage service  for every bit of data that a user  uploads  and this is what allows it to be half  the cost of amazon glacier  so i would encourage uh everyone to  check out  the cold stack website you can read more  about how the ecosystem works you can  read the light paper  they actually have a great live demo  where you can upload some test files  from your computer  see how the cold stack interface works  you can check out the road map to see  how they're getting to the final product  launch near the end of this year and  there's some really  interesting partnerships you can look at  as well cold stack is a project  i'm keeping an eye on it'll be  interesting to see everything as it  rolls  out over the course of this year and the  decentralized cloud storage industry  altogether has a market cap  of about five billion dollars all around  decentralized cloud storage is an  interesting space to follow  data storage is a very cool application  of blockchain technology  and i've put the link to the cold stack  website in the description of this video  for you to check out what they're up to  as always with any project with anything  that involves finances with anything  that involves money  i'm not making any endorsement or  suggestion that anybody  invest in any particular way i'm telling  you about the project as i see it  and everybody should be doing all due  diligence before making  any financially impactful decision
 

